---
import Page from '../../layouts/Page.astro';
import WorkedExample from '../../components/WorkedExample.astro';
---
<Page
  title="Ontology"
  description="ArborSpace turns raw tables into linked business objects, starting from a domain model you adapt rather than build."
  eyebrow="Product · Ontology"
  heading="Your vocabulary, as objects and links."
  lead="The ontology turns raw tables into business objects (an asset, an engagement, a supplier, a site) linked together, which teams and agents act on directly."
>
  <section>
    <div class="wrap split">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>Not a blank page</h2>
        <p>
          General-purpose platforms can build ontologies, but rarely ship a ready-to-use domain
          model: it is up to the client to build it. An expert firm has neither the budget nor the
          team to model its business from scratch.
        </p>
        <p>
          ArborSpace ships with a first model of the domain (energy assets, due diligence
          engagements) that the firm adapts rather than builds.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>What the firm declares</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Asset classes</strong>, such as a class 7F gas turbine.</li>
          <li><strong>Engagements</strong>, such as a technical due diligence.</li>
          <li><strong>Stakeholders</strong>, such as the lender financing an asset.</li>
          <li><strong>Relationships</strong> between them: installed at, assessed in, delivered to.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="alt">
    <div class="wrap"><WorkedExample /></div>
  </section>
</Page>
